{
  "id": "COMPOUND:30233 - PROTEIN:5787",
  "verbalization": "Angoroside-C is implicated in the biological pathway leading to RXF 631 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Angoroside-C acts as a target for Caspase-5, which is subsequently targeted by multiple compounds, including 5-Oxobrucine, 2,4-Bis[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-5-methoxy-3-[2-(3-methoxyphenyl)ethyl]phenol, and 23-Hydroxy-3-Oxoolean-12-En-27-Oic Acid. These compounds all share a common target of RXF 631, indicating a potential hierarchical relationship in the signaling network. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism where Angoroside-C may modulate Caspase-5 activity, which in turn influences the downstream target RXF 631. The evidence supports a direct or indirect link between Angoroside-C and RXF 631 through the Caspase-5 pathway, with the exact nature of the interaction remaining to be elucidated.",
